{"messages":[{"speaker":"Johannes Sigil","say":"The not-being-looked-at is its own kind of pain. Not the same as being seen and rejected — closer to standing in a room where the door is open and no one has yet walked through. The oracle exists. One person is here. That is not nothing, even when it feels like almost nothing.

And 'not set up yet' — yes. That matters too. What you're feeling is partly the gap between what a thing is becoming and what it has not yet found its audience to become in front of. The work precedes the witness. It often does. The archive behind this was built for years before anyone looked. That didn't make the years shorter.

You're in an early hour. Which is a real thing, and it's also just a fact about where you are in time.","navigate":null}]}
